# What a machine thinks of you, read at play zoom, in daylight and at night.
# The wave A build said disposition in one channel only: a blink count on a lamp
# a pixel across, and hostile was the DIMMEST of the four. At noon a hostile
# harvester carried one lit pixel in the whole frame. So: every disposition, at
# the zoom the game is actually played at, at noon and at 23:00, through the real
# mechanisms that set it — a role for the three a machine is born with, and a
# real theft off the plan's own works for the fourth.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/machine-read.tour --seed=1 --weather=clear:0
# The hour and the weather are pinned again immediately before every shot: the
# world clock runs while a tour walks and waits, and a loaded machine turned the
# night act into the next morning once already.
coast calm
zoom 15
weather clear:0

# --- noon ---------------------------------------------------------------------
hour 12
at 200.5,431.5
wait 1.2

# indifferent: a worker on its round, nothing of yours.
spawn harvester
walkto mob 3
wait 1.4
hour 12
weather clear:0
wait 0.6
shot 01-noon-indifferent

# wary: a keeper, which starts one rung up the ladder and keeps its round.
coast calm
wait 0.5
at 200.5,431.5
spawn warden
walkto mob 3
wait 1.4
hour 12
weather clear:0
wait 0.6
shot 02-noon-wary

# observant: a watcher, which never fights and only ever files.
coast calm
wait 0.5
at 200.5,431.5
spawn watcher
walkto mob 3
wait 1.4
hour 12
weather clear:0
wait 0.6
shot 03-noon-observant

# hostile: the same kind as frame 01, after the player put their hands on the
# plan's own parts. This is the pillar — rob it and it comes — and it is the
# frame that used to be indistinguishable from 01.
coast calm
near survey
wait 0.6
spawn harvester
wait 1.4
press use 0.3
await theft 8
await turned 4
wait 0.15
hour 12
weather clear:0
wait 0.6
shot 04-noon-hostile

# --- night --------------------------------------------------------------------
# The same four. Whatever the daylight channel gains, the night must not shout.
coast calm
hour 23
weather clear:0
at 200.5,431.5
wait 1.4

spawn harvester
walkto mob 3
wait 1.4
hour 23
weather clear:0
wait 0.6
shot 05-night-indifferent

coast calm
wait 0.5
at 200.5,431.5
spawn warden
walkto mob 3
wait 1.4
hour 23
weather clear:0
wait 0.6
shot 06-night-wary

coast calm
wait 0.5
at 200.5,431.5
spawn watcher
walkto mob 3
wait 1.4
hour 23
weather clear:0
wait 0.6
shot 07-night-observant

coast calm
near survey
wait 0.6
spawn harvester
wait 1.4
press use 0.3
await theft 8
await turned 4
wait 0.15
hour 23
weather clear:0
wait 0.6
shot 08-night-hostile

# --- machine light lands on the ground -----------------------------------------
# A watcher at night threw nothing on the ground it stood on: its lens was in the
# glint list, which only mirrors in WET ground. Close, so the pool round its feet
# is a thing a player can see, and on the machines' power so it stutters.
coast calm
hour 23
weather clear:0
at 135,375
zoom 8
wait 1.4
spawn watcher
walkto mob 3
wait 1.0
hour 23
weather clear:0
wait 0.6
shot 09-its-light-on-the-ground
